title: Women's Rights
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: CHP_in_government = 1 and womens_rights_timer = 0 and chancellor_party == "CHP"
on-arrival: womens_rights_timer += 8; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/portraits/ikd.jpg
frequency: 50


= Women's Rights

The achievements in terms of women's rights are one of our proudest memories of Atatürk's reforms. Women were given the right of equal education as men in 1924, given equal status in marriages and the right of unrestricted divorce with the modern Turkish civil code in 1926 and given the right to vote and to be elected in 1934, 10 years earlier than even in France. However despite these previous legal achievements, there is a lot that needs to be done in order to achieve full gender inequality in an age where these rights are increasingly coming under scrutiny by the reactionary right. 

[? if MSP_in_government == 1 : However, women's rights reforms while we are in a coalition with the Islamists will incur significant coalition dissent! ?]

- @legalize: Legalize abortions on request, which used to be outlawed, until the 10th week of pregnancy.
- @legalize2: Extend the availability of abortions on request by offering them in all state-owned hospitals.
- @labor: Announce directives for establishing equal pay for equal work, regardless of gender.
- @maternity: Standardize paid maternity leaves. 
- @maternity1: Work on extending the standardized maternity leaves from 16 weeks to 24 weeks.
- @maternity2: Extend the maternity leaves to 24 weeks.
- @guvenlik: Move to include housewives, housemaids and servants in the social security network.
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@legalize
view-if: legalizee == 0
on-arrival: women_reform += 0.2; legalizee += 1; coalition_dissent -= 1 if MSP_in_government == 1; state_employees_chp += 1; if koykent_progress >= 5 then rural_chp += 1; petty_bourgeoisie_chp += 1; workers_chp += 1; if koykent_progress < 5 then rural_chp -= 1; MSP_relation -= 10; z_relation -= 5

We have legalized abortions on request until the 10th week of pregnancy, the farthest point we could reasonably push for, so that no women is prevented from making decisions about her own body. [? if koykent_progress < 5 : While the largely urban population approves of this reform, we unfortunately cant break the reactionary sentiments within the ruralty yet without a radical land reform.?]

[? if MSP_in_government == 1 : Delegates from the MSP decry the achievements of this reform calling it "murder" and "immoral", damaging the stability of our coalition.?]

@legalize2
subtitle: -1 budget.
view-if: legalizee == 1
choose-if: legalizee == 1 and budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if budget < 1 : Requires 1 budget.?] [? if legalizee != 1 : We have already legalized abortions until the 10th week of pregnancy and made them widely available!?]
on-arrival: women_reform += 0.4; budget -= 1; legalizee += 1; coalition_dissent -= 1 if MSP_in_government == 1; state_employees_chp += 1; if koykent_progress >= 5 then rural_chp += 1; petty_bourgeoisie_CHP += 1; workers_CHP += 1; MSP_relation -= 10; z_relation -= 5

Offering abortions on demand across the nation gives women control over their own body and their reproductive rights, improving women's rights significantly. [? if koykent_progress < 5 : While the largely urban population approves of this reform, we unfortunately cant break the reactionary sentiments within the ruralty yet without a radical land reform.?]

[? if MSP_in_government == 1 : Delegates from the MSP decry the achievements of this reform calling it "murder" and "immoral", damaging the stability of our coalition.?]

@labor
choose-if: labor_minister_party = "CHP"
unavailable-subtitle: We need the Labour Ministry for this action!
on-arrival: women_reform += 0.2; growth_modifier -= 0.2; inflation_modifier += 0.2; workers_chp += 4; state_employees_chp += 4; petty_bourgeoisie -= 1; capitalists_chp -= 5

Even though men and women may be putting the same labour and contributed the same amount of revenue to a company, women are often paid less due to societal prejudices. Even though equal pay for equal work wont be achieved in one step, we have to continue our efforts.

@maternity
subtitle: -1 budget.
choose-if: labor_minister_party = "CHP"
unavailable-subtitle: [? if labor_minister_party != "CHP" : We need the Labour Ministry for this action!?]  [? if budget < 1 : Requires 1 budget.?]
view-if: maternityy == 0
on-arrival: women_reform += 0.2; growth_modifier -= 0.1; workers_chp += 3; state_employees_chp += 3; petty_bourgeoisie_chp -= 1; budget -= 1; maternityy += 1

A maternity leave of 16 weeks is given to working women, 8 prenatal and 8 postnatal. Thanks to this reform now women do not have to depend on the mercy of their predominantly male employers to manage their familial affairs. However we can further increase the duration of the leave if we concentrate our efforts.

@maternity1
view-if: maternityy == 1
choose-if: labor_minister_party = "CHP"
unavailable-subtitle: We need the Labour Ministry for this action!
on-arrival: maternityy += 1

We work on extending the maternity leave from 16 weeks to 24 weeks in cooperation with the Labour Ministry.

@maternity2
subtitle: -1 budget.
choose-if: labor_minister_party = "CHP" and maternityy == 2 and budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if labor_minister_party != "CHP" : We need the Labour Ministry for this action!?] [? if maternity != 2 : We have already established an extended maternity leave of 24 weeks!?]  [? if budget < 1 : Requires 1 budget.?]
view-if: maternityy >= 2
on-arrival: women_reform += 0.4; growth_modifier -= 0.1; workers_chp += 3; state_employees_chp += 3; petty_bourgeoisie_chp -= 1; budget -= 1; maternityy += 1

We extend the maternal leave to 24 weeks, securing a length period which women can dedicate to their newborn children and household without financial pressure from the greedy employers. 

@guvenlik
subtitle: -1 budget.
choose-if: budget >= 1 and guvenlikk == 0
unavailable-subtitle:  [? if budget < 1 : Requires 1 budget.?] [? if guvenlikk != 0 : We have already extended social security services to financially vulnerable women!?]
on-arrival: women_reform += 0.2; budget -= 1; workers_chp += 3; state_employees_chp += 2; petty_bourgeoisie_chp += 1; guvenlikk += 1

We move to include housewives, maids and servants in the social security services; giving women working in households greater independence from their husbands and employers.
